invariant: INV-69
file: src/keccak_neon.c
catches: keccak_neon_equiv_test
reason: keccak_neon_block reads lane i of state 0 whatever k names, so
  both entries of a pair take the first stream. The equivalence test
  compares each state's blocks with sha3.c's stream for its own
  indices.

--- old
        uint64_t lane = s->lane[i][k];
--- new
        uint64_t lane = s->lane[i][k & 0];
